 "about": "OpenArm 1.0's parallel gripper (openarm_description's parallel_link end effector, the v1.0 arm's; OpenArm 2.0's gripper is another, its pinch_gripper, not drawn here) at full opening: openarm_description 81fe647, assets/robot/openarm_v1.0/urdf/example/v1.urdf (Apache-2.0, Enactic): finger_joint1/2 prismatic 0..0.044 m, finger_joint2 mimicking finger_joint1, q 44 mm.  The bodies are the hand (hand.dae: the guide rail, its sheet-metal ends and the plate on the motor), the gripper's motor (link7.dae's components above its wrist bracket: the can, its end caps and screws; the bracket is not drawn) and, under each finger, the guide's carriage block (finger.dae's material mat_0.009), where the URDF places them.  The Library mesh is the HandUMI replica of the OpenArm 1.0 finger (handumi-hw 1448278, OpenArmv1/OpenArm-left.stl, Apache-2.0), registered on finger.dae's finger (the rotation from the faces' normals, the translation by nearest points; median 0.001 mm: Enactic's finger surface (Apache-2.0, Enactic, Inc.) but for the mount at its base).  The other finger is the URDF's right finger: the same finger turned 180 degrees about the hand's axis (its visual's yaw pi), so its sensor is the same board.  The looks: drawn after Enactic's own pictures of the OpenArm 1.0 gripper (2026-11-17: openarm.dev's social-preview photo (its og:image, ogp.webp) of the bimanual OpenArm 1.0, both grippers in it, and the 1.0 documentation's gripper renders, docs.openarm.dev/1.0, its gripper pages and bill of materials): matte black printed fingers (the Library's part, the HandUMI replica of the OpenArm finger), a black motor can between bright machined aluminium end caps, the bent stainless sheet-metal brackets and the plate on the motor, the guide's stainless carriage blocks under the fingers, and the dark guide rail with its bright counterbored holes; the CAD files' own colours (finger.dae's black finger and pale carriage, hand.dae's dark rail and pale plate, link7.dae's dark can and pale caps) agree.  Not modelled: the swivel rotor and its two links (not in openarm_description's v1.0 meshes), the wrist bracket under the motor (link7.dae's, left out), the cables.",
